        "text": "According to Attorney General of New York, the dispute centers on whether the OCC\u2019s regulations pre\u2011empt state antidiscrimination and consumer\u2011protection laws, thereby barring the New\u202fYork Attorney General from enforcing those laws against national banks."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Office of the Comptroller of the Currency",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9f07fefe037bbece22d31c6c78fc93a4386521ce2fa4c22b147d8e2962a925cd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9f07fefe037b-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, the Office of the Comptroller maintains that the OCC regulations expressly pre\u2011empt any state enforcement authority."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "The Clearing House Association",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9f07fefe037bbece22d31c6c78fc93a4386521ce2fa4c22b147d8e2962a925cd",
            "evidence_ids": [
